  "nl_text": "The schemabench_0086 database contains five tables: subscriptions, users, subscription_items, receipts, and tax_rates. The subscriptions table stores information about user subscriptions, including the user's ID, subscription name, Stripe ID, status, price, quantity, trial end date, end date, and update and creation timestamps. The users table contains information about the users, including their Stripe ID, payment method type, last four digits of their payment method, expiration date, extra billing information, trial end date, billing address, billing address line 2, billing city, billing state, billing postal code, billing country, VAT ID, and receipt emails. The subscription_items table contains information about the items in a subscription, including the subscription ID, Stripe ID, product, price, quantity, and update and creation timestamps. The receipts table contains information about the receipts, including the user ID, provider ID, amount, tax, paid date, update and creation timestamps. The tax_rates table contains information about the tax rates, including the Stripe ID, percentage, and update and creation timestamps. The subscriptions table has a foreign key relationship with the users table, and the subscription_items table has a foreign key relationship with the subscriptions table. The receipts table has a foreign key relationship with the users table. The tax_rates table has no foreign key relationships.",
  "gold_question": "1) Background / Context\n\nThe project aims to develop a subscription billing solution built on Laravel, leveraging the Laravel Cashier package. This system targets SaaS businesses, facilitating subscription management through an integrated billing portal using Stripe and Paddle. The system simplifies recurring billing and customer invoice management, serving as a robust starting point for new SaaS applications.\n\n 2) Objectives\n\n- Develop a comprehensive subscription billing system for Laravel-based applications.\n- Enable easy management of subscription plans and customer billing.\n- Support multiple payment providers, including Stripe and Paddle, to handle transactions.\n- Provide a flexible billing experience for customers, including per-seat billing options.\n\n 3) Stakeholders & Users\n\n- SaaS Business Owners: Individuals or entities looking to implement subscription billing in their applications.\n- Customers: Users subscribing to SaaS services and managing their billing information via the portal.\n- Developers: Software engineers who will integrate and manage the billing system within their SaaS platforms.\n\n 4) Functional Descriptions\n\n- Subscription Management: Define and manage monthly or yearly subscription plans via a configuration file.\n- Customer Billing Portal: Provide a standalone portal where customers can subscribe to or modify plans, update payment methods, and download invoices.\n- Invoice Handling: Automatically generate and email PDF invoices to customers for each billing cycle.\n- Payment Provider Support: Integrate with Paddle to accept payments, including PayPal, enhancing payment flexibility.\n- Per-Seat Billing: Implement the capability to charge customers based on the number of team members or projects.\n- Frontend Flexibility: Maintain an isolated billing portal frontend, allowing the main application frontend to use any preferred technology stack.\n- System Upgrades: Ensure straightforward updates to the system without interfering with the core application code.\n\n 5) Non-Functional Descriptions\n\n- Scalability: Support an increasing number of customers and subscription transactions efficiently.\n- Security: Ensure secure handling of payment information and comply with relevant regulatory standards.\n- Usability: Provide an intuitive user interface in the billing portal for seamless interaction.\n- Extensibility: Allow future enhancements and integrations without significant rework of the existing system.",
  "input_json": "/data/SchemaBench/Experiment/schema2text_codellama13b/0086.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: schemabench_0086\nCREATE TABLE `subscriptions` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `subscription_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `stripe_id` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `status` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `price` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  `quantity` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `trial_end_date` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `end_date` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,\n  `updated_at` datetime NOT NULL DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP ON UPDATE CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `subscriptions_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `users` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `stripe_id` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `payment_method_type` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `last_four_digits` char(4) NOT NULL,\n  `expiration_date` date DEFAULT NULL,\n  `extra_billing_info` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `trial_end_date` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `billing_address` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `billing_address_line_2` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `billing_city` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  `billing_state` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  `billing_postal_code` varchar(20) NOT NULL,\n  `billing_country` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  `vat_id` varchar(100) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `receipt_emails` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `subscription_items` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `subscription_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `stripe_id` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `product` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `price` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  `quantity` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,\n  `updated_at` datetime NOT NULL DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP ON UPDATE CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `subscription_items_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`subscription_id`) REFERENCES `subscriptions` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `receipts` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `provider_id` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `amount` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  `tax` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  `paid_date` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,\n  `updated_at` datetime NOT NULL DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP ON UPDATE CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `receipts_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `tax_rates` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `stripe_id` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `percentage` decimal(5,2) NOT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,\n  `updated_at` datetime NOT NULL DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP ON UPDATE CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
